  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1215 AM MDT Thu Jul 30 2026\n\nThe backdoor front is modeled to spread west to the AZ border late\nFriday night into Saturday morning, replenishing moisture across\nwestern NM and setting the stage for a more active day across \ncentral NM. Increasing northerly flow aloft will keep Saturday's \ncrop of storms moving at a decent clip, but with an increased \nthreat for severe storms as both shear and instability trend up \nmore. In addition, the threat for burn scar flooding will trend up\nSaturday given the potential for training storms and higher \nrainfall rates anticipated from robust convection. Moisture is \nforecast to mix-out across far western NM Saturday and a Heat \nAdvisory may be required for the Northwest Plateau given the \nanomalously strong Monsoon high over eastern AZ. The Monsoon high\nis forecast to weaken some Sun/Mon, with drier air aloft wrapping\naround the circulation and working south across our area bringing\na downtick in daily rounds of storms. With the the downtrend in\nPWATs and lower storm coverage, heat gets cranked back up and more\nHeat Advisories may be required Mon/Tue for the lower elevations.\nThe mean forecast centering of the Monsoon high is over the Four\nCorners from mid through late next week, with a continued mix of\nheat impacts and thunderstorm impacts expected across northern and\ncentral NM.",
